emy King, controls the center, and clears the path for immediate short castling.\n\nReason: The move B: f1-c4 develops a key piece to an aggressive square without hindering the defense of the central d4 pawn. It prepares for castling, which is crucial in such an open position, and exerts pressure on the Black position by eyeing the weak f7 square and controlling the center.\n\nAnswer: B: f1-c4"}
